  "body": "Found in M5's review of PR #1668 (#1659). The review did not block on it.\n\n## What happens\n\n`crosses_rim` (`crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs`) counts a pass through a loop vertex as a rim crossing when the vertex's two neighbours lie on opposite sides of the move. The test is the exact sign `su * sw < 0`, with no zero band.\n\nAssume a wall that runs along the trace and wobbles by about 1e-6 mm. Its vertices then sit on alternate sides of the move. The check reads this as a crossing, and the wall check excuses the move.\n\n## Expected\n\nA crossing needs each neighbour off the trace line by at least a small distance, for example `CROSSING_TOUCH`. A neighbour nearer than that counts as on the line, and the move answers to the walls as before.\n\n## Also\n\nThe arc branch of `Trace::through` (`crates/sim/src/verify/arc_wall.rs`) has no direct pin.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A pin for a wall along the trace with a wobble below the band. The move still answers to the walls.\n- A pin for a true crossing with neighbours beyond the band. The move crosses.\n- A pin for the arc branch of `Trace::through`.\n",
